  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3788",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine appears to interact with potassium channels through a shared mechanism involving delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. The evidence suggests that Guanidine binds to Kcna6, Kcnv2, and Kcna7, all of which participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity, which is ultimately associated with Kcns2. This indicates that Guanidine may influence Kcns2 through a common pathway involving potassium channel activity. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, with Guanidine potentially modulating Kcns2 via the delayed rectifier potassium channel. The overlapping roles of these potassium channel subunits in the same biological process support the idea that Guanidine's effects on Kcns2 are mediated through a shared cellular mechanism.",
